{"entryId":"3340","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:3340:1","sourceSha256":"4e49197057ec3c1be8d7600161707d83a092d84ae553180ac9fa13afe1621dd5","englishSha256":"a4429114f52607cf1702c0b42c0af4b49bf2d888754370798112880ca75bc687","citations":[{"id":"3340:1:link-018","he":[27,64],"en":[81,98],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_49a.8"},"reference":"Chullin 49a:8","assessment":"The exact Chullin report names his father as one of Rafram’s resh kallei; Rashi says these are leading expositors who projected his teaching to the public.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 49a:8","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_49a.8"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Chullin 49a:8:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Chullin_49a.8.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3340:1:link-019","he":[195,233],"en":[567,584],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_59b.6"},"reference":"Chullin 59b:6","assessment":"Chullin gives both the decision favoring Shmuel and the instruction about Aḥai. Rashi is the precise source of the parenthetical explanation, which should retain its own voice.","evidence":[{"reference":"Chullin 59b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_59b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Chullin 59b:7","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_59b.7"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Rashi on Chullin 59b:7:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Chullin_59b.7.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]},{"id":"3340:1:link-027","he":[138,159],"en":[235,296],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Proverbs_18.20"},"reference":"Proverbs 18:20","assessment":"The quotation is the first half of Proverbs 18:20.","evidence":[{"reference":"Proverbs 18:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Proverbs_18.20"},"witness":"Miqra according to the Masorah"},{"reference":"Chullin 59b:6","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Chullin_59b.6"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"3340:1:link-028","he":[235,278],"en":[446,511],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Chullin_59b.7.1"},"reference":"Rashi on Chullin 59b:7:1","assessment":"The wording of this parenthetical belongs to Rashi’s explanation of honoring Aḥai.","evidence":[{"reference":"Rashi on Chullin 59b:7:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Chullin_59b.7.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,2,1,3],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Rashi describes the resh kallei as leading expositors who made Rafram’s teaching heard by the audience.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
